  "activeSceneId": "id-sr1mf4dwxfj-mv0hah5h",
  "year": 1914,
  "era": "World Wars",
  "width": 720,
  "height": 1280,
  "fps": 30,
  "assets": [],
  "scripts": {
    "project": "Noveria History short-form library. Each video is designed for roughly 35–50 seconds of narration with vertical 9:16 visuals.",
    "sceneById": {
      "id-sr1mf4dwxfj-mv0hah5h": "Germany’s 1914 plan drove through Belgium toward France. But French and British forces stopped the advance at the First Battle of the Marne.",
      "id-5dqowapueza-mv0hah5i": "Both sides then tried to outflank each other northward. By late 1914, trenches stretched from the North Sea toward Switzerland.",
      "id-eq9yv69hy14-mv0hah5i": "Machine guns, artillery, barbed wire, and deep defenses made crossing open ground brutally expensive. Huge offensives often gained little ground.",
      "id-56t2zt7v77-mv0hah5i": "Germany’s spring offensives advanced in 1918, but they failed to force a decision. Allied counterattacks, reinforced by growing American forces, pushed the front back.",
      "id-fzgufekzvx9-mv0hah5i": "The Allied Hundred Days offensive kept pressure on Germany. With its army exhausted and allies collapsing, Germany accepted the armistice on November 11, 1918.",
      "id-8vhr1vbu3gv-mv0hah5i": "In the east, armies fought across a far larger area than in France and Belgium. That made one continuous trench wall much harder to maintain.",
      "id-w0fny2gbs0b-mv0hah5i": "Russia invaded East Prussia in 1914. Germany surrounded and defeated one Russian army at Tannenberg, while fighting continued farther south against Austria-Hungary.",
      "id-6diz2osdhp8-mv0hah5i": "In 1915, the Central Powers broke through at Gorlice–Tarnów. Russian armies retreated far east, giving up large territories in Poland and beyond.",
      "id-j32cyvx9qae-mv0hah5i": "The 1916 Brusilov Offensive smashed much of Austria-Hungary’s front and forced Germany to send help east, but Russia paid heavily too.",
      "id-ilegovl5psh-mv0hah5i": "Revolution shattered the Russian war effort in 1917. The Bolshevik government signed the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk in March 1918, ending Russia’s participation.",
      "id-3gdo6pgbpfj-mv0hah5i": "Japan had been expanding through China and Southeast Asia. In 1941, after Japan moved into southern Indochina, the United States froze Japanese assets and effectively cut off access to American oil.",
      "id-ew25wkxo0zp-mv0hah5i": "Japan chose a surprise carrier strike to cripple the U.S. Pacific Fleet while Japanese forces moved toward resource-rich territories farther south.",
      "id-q5q5j5ksjy-mv0hah5i": "On the morning of December 7, Japanese aircraft hit Pearl Harbor. In less than two hours, more than 2,400 Americans were killed and numerous ships and aircraft were destroyed or damaged.",
      "id-td1m9pwxrx-mv0hah5i": "No American aircraft carriers were in Pearl Harbor that morning. Japan also left major fuel storage and repair facilities intact, helping the U.S. recover faster than Japan hoped.",
      "id-hx4t4jinbom-mv0hah5i": "The United States declared war on Japan the next day. Germany and Italy declared war on the United States days later, turning America fully into a global war.",
      "id-xlwlguqscb-mv0hah5i": "In June 1942, Japan aimed to seize Midway and draw the U.S. Pacific Fleet into a battle where it could be destroyed.",
      "id-dn52y1wfmk7-mv0hah5i": "American codebreakers had identified Midway as the target. Admiral Nimitz positioned U.S. carriers northeast of the atoll to surprise the Japanese fleet.",
      "id-gxlclk4g4vj-mv0hah5i": "On June 4, Japanese aircraft attacked Midway. While Japanese decks were busy rearming and refueling, American carrier aircraft found the fleet.",
      "id-etsn3rr2f38-mv0hah5i": "U.S. dive bombers struck three Japanese carriers within minutes; a fourth was hit later. Japan lost Akagi, Kaga, Soryu, and Hiryu.",
      "id-0q386b829ytb-mv0hah5i": "Midway did not end the Pacific War, but it destroyed much of Japan’s elite carrier striking force and shifted the strategic initiative toward the United States.",
      "id-o2uv63wbzt-mv0hah5i": "On June 6, 1944, Allied forces launched Operation Overlord—the invasion of Nazi-occupied France across the English Channel.",
      "id-kipglub863-mv0hah5i": "Before the beach landings, American and British airborne troops dropped behind German defenses to seize roads, bridges, and key positions.",
      "id-mxk7kz5ch0o-mv0hah5i": "The seaborne assault hit five beaches: Utah and Omaha for the Americans, Gold and Sword for the British, and Juno for the Canadians.",
      "id-wbqdsykxhsr-mv0hah5i": "The Allies did not achieve every first-day objective, and fighting was especially costly at Omaha. But they secured beachheads that Germany could not throw back into the sea.",
      "id-ss4gkqtf14-mv0hah5i": "The Normandy lodgment opened the Western Front in Europe. Over the following weeks, Allied armies built up strength and began the campaign to liberate France.",
      "id-vkk2qtjd019-mv0hah5i": "After the Seven Years’ War, Britain faced huge debts and tried to raise more revenue from its American colonies. New taxes and tighter imperial control triggered resistance.",
      "id-7azizh0yrmu-mv0hah5i": "Many colonists argued Parliament was taxing them without their consent. The Stamp Act, Townshend duties, Boston Massacre, and Tea Party deepened the crisis.",
      "id-5nso4mrgshi-mv0hah5j": "In April 1775, fighting broke out at Lexington and Concord. The conflict quickly grew from a political crisis into an armed rebellion.",
      "id-w07qdfjrw4j-mv0hah5j": "The colonies declared independence in July 1776. After the American victory at Saratoga, France entered the war as an American ally in 1778.",
      "id-b68n0dqq72-mv0hah5j": "British forces surrendered at Yorktown in 1781 after American and French forces trapped Cornwallis. The Treaty of Paris in 1783 formally recognized U.S. independence.",
      "id-hgy3y58aevv-mv0hah5j": "By 1789, France had heavy state debt, an unfair tax system, and a severe economic crisis. Rising bread prices made anger even worse.",
      "id-t4hbxmc5ph-mv0hah5j": "Louis XVI called the Estates-General. Representatives of the Third Estate declared themselves the National Assembly and claimed the right to write a constitution.",
      "id-pwdlncnewnm-mv0hah5j": "On July 14, 1789, a Paris crowd stormed the Bastille. The prison held few inmates, but its fall became a powerful symbol of royal authority collapsing.",
      "id-9pcgx3ya9xe-mv0hah5j": "Revolutionary governments abolished feudal privileges and issued the Declaration of the Rights of Man. In 1792 France became a republic; Louis XVI was executed in 1793.",
      "id-xiyxu1brh4-mv0hah5j": "The revolution radicalized into the Reign of Terror, then shifted to the Directory. In 1799, Napoleon Bonaparte seized power in a coup, ending this phase of the revolution.",
      "id-amcfj3xzy3f-mv0hah5j": "Napoleon escaped exile on Elba in 1815 and returned to power. European states immediately formed a new coalition to remove him.",
      "id-uku9vi5wvoo-mv0hah5j": "Napoleon moved into Belgium hoping to defeat Wellington’s Anglo-Allied army and Blücher’s Prussians before they could fully unite.",
      "id-spwcr0msfps-mv0hah5j": "On June 16, Napoleon defeated the Prussians at Ligny, but they were not destroyed. Nearby, French forces failed to decisively dislodge Wellington at Quatre Bras.",
      "id-q1w75k6qpp-mv0hah5j": "On June 18, Napoleon attacked Wellington at Waterloo. Late in the day, Blücher’s Prussians arrived on the French flank, while Wellington’s line still held.",
      "id-qoy0muj0ckk-mv0hah5j": "A final French attack failed, and Napoleon’s army broke. He abdicated again and was sent to Saint Helena. Waterloo ended his rule for good.",
      "id-amtn148bb24-mv0hah5j": "After the failed Bay of Pigs invasion, the Soviet Union secretly placed nuclear missiles in Cuba, partly to deter another U.S. invasion.",
      "id-9iu29ogb0mt-mv0hah5j": "On October 14, a U.S. U-2 photographed missile sites in Cuba. President Kennedy was briefed on October 16, beginning the crisis inside the White House.",
      "id-0ra7j5uerks-mv0hah5j": "Kennedy chose a naval quarantine rather than an immediate air strike. U.S. ships moved to block additional offensive weapons from reaching Cuba.",
      "id-sxvpsqlowkf-mv0hah5j": "Tension peaked on October 27: a U-2 was shot down over Cuba while U.S. and Soviet leaders exchanged messages and searched for a way out.",
      "id-jezu64ywm9p-mv0hah5j": "Khrushchev agreed to remove Soviet missiles from Cuba. The United States publicly pledged not to invade Cuba and secretly agreed to remove Jupiter missiles from Turkey.",
      "id-ou1sryge0p-mv0hah5j": "After World War II, Germany and Berlin were divided. By 1961, East Germany had lost large numbers of people through West Berlin, creating a political and economic crisis.",
      "id-2ycxst9gx49-mv0hah5j": "On August 13, East German authorities sealed the border. Barbed wire quickly became concrete walls, guard towers, and a fortified barrier through Berlin.",
      "id-c27ecj6f3m-mv0hah5j": "The wall divided streets, workplaces, and families. People still tried to escape, while U.S. and Soviet tanks even faced each other at Checkpoint Charlie in 1961.",
      "id-xcvwqj2oa1d-mv0hah5j": "By 1989, reforms in the Soviet bloc, mass protests in East Germany, and new escape routes through neighboring countries put enormous pressure on the regime.",
      "id-0r78lx178yb-mv0hah5j": "On November 9, a confused announcement about new travel rules sent crowds to border crossings. Guards opened the gates, and Berliners began tearing the wall down. Germany reunified in 1990."
    }
  },
